INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(614,'http://www.eumetsat.int/features/meteosat-third-generation-4d','https://eumetsat.int/features/meteosat-third-generation-4d','Meteosat Third Generation in 4D','meteosatthirdgenerationin4d','eumetsat','EUMETSAT news','en','2026-10-13T08:49:36Z','2026-10-17T08:55:16Z','Meteosat Third Generation in 4D Craig MacDonald Tue, 13/10/2026 - 10:49 Watch as Meteosat Third Generation captures storms taking shape in four dimensions As Meteosat-13 enters operational service, an animation combines data from MTG sounder and imager instruments for a stunning view into the atmosphere On 20 August 2026, with temperatures above 40°C in parts of the Mediterranean, hot, humid air met cooler air arriving from the Atlantic. Over the next two days, severe thunderstorms broke out across southern and central Europe. Floods and landslides cut off mountain villages in northern Italy, ',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(615,'http://www.eumetsat.int/image-week-dust-cloud-moves-over-mediterranean','https://eumetsat.int/image-week-dust-cloud-moves-over-mediterranean','Image of the week: Dust cloud moves over the Mediterranean','imageoftheweekdustcloudmovesoverthemediterranean','eumetsat','EUMETSAT news','en','2026-10-09T07:00:00Z','2026-10-17T08:55:16Z','Image of the week: Dust cloud moves over the Mediterranean Sarah Leach Fri, 09/10/2026 - 09:00 Image of the week: Dust cloud moves over the Mediterranean Watching our Earth from space This week’s image is of Saharan dust moving northeast across the Mediterranean Sea on 25 August 2026. The image was captured by the Meteosat-12 geostationary weather satellite 36,000km above the Earth. Last Updated Published on Saharan dust particles are lifted into the atmosphere by gusts of surface wind and can be transported and deposited thousands of kilometres away. When dust travels over populated areas, it',2.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(616,'http://www.eumetsat.int/sentinel-3c-first-images','https://eumetsat.int/sentinel-3c-first-images','Sentinel-3C first images','sentinel3cfirstimages','eumetsat','EUMETSAT news','en','2026-10-08T12:30:00Z','2026-10-17T08:55:16Z','Sentinel-3C first images Sarah Leach Thu, 08/10/2026 - 14:30 Copernicus Sentinel-3C sends its spectacular first images of Earth The third satellite launched on the Copernicus Sentinel-3 mission delivers its captivating first images Copernicus Sentinel-3C, a new satellite built to measure the colour, height and temperature of Earth’s oceans, land and ice, has sent back its first images from space. Last Updated Published on The very first image stretches from southern Germany to North Africa, with Italy and the Mediterranean Sea at its centre under largely clear skies. Captured from 30 September',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(617,'https://aiforgood.itu.int/india-mobile-congress-2026-connecting-ai-innovation-skills-and-real-world-impact/','https://aiforgood.itu.int/india-mobile-congress-2026-connecting-ai-innovation-skills-and-real-world-impact','India Mobile Congress 2026: Connecting AI innovation, skills and real-world impact','indiamobilecongress2026connectingaiinnovationskillsandrealworldimpact','itu_ai4good','ITU AI for Good','en','2026-10-13T15:34:09Z','2026-10-17T08:55:20Z','India Mobile Congress 2026 brought together young innovators, researchers, policymakers and international organisations in New Delhi to explore how AI can deliver practical benefits for people. The post India Mobile Congress 2026: Connecting AI innovation, skills and real-world impact appeared first on AI for Good .',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(618,'https://aiforgood.itu.int/trust-isnt-coded-it-must-be-designed-into-the-ecosystem/','https://aiforgood.itu.int/trust-isnt-coded-it-must-be-designed-into-the-ecosystem','Trust isn’t coded – it must be designed into the ecosystem','trustisntcoded','itu_ai4good','ITU AI for Good','en','2026-10-12T12:00:36Z','2026-10-17T08:55:20Z','AI may be powered by code, but its ability to create sustained value for people depends on the ecosystems built around it. As AI moves from experimentation to scale, trust must become a system capability – connecting data, governance, operational oversight and partnerships across institutional boundaries. The post Trust isn’t coded – it must be designed into the ecosystem appeared first on AI for Good .',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(619,'https://aiforgood.itu.int/why-we-were-at-ai-for-good-grounding-artificial-intelligence-in-knowledge-you-can-trust/','https://aiforgood.itu.int/why-we-were-at-ai-for-good-grounding-artificial-intelligence-in-knowledge-you-can-trust','Why we were at AI for Good: grounding artificial intelligence in knowledge you can trust','whywewereataiforgoodgroundingartificialintelligenceinknowledgeyoucantrust','itu_ai4good','ITU AI for Good','en','2026-10-09T12:00:44Z','2026-10-17T08:55:20Z','Ask anyone building or using AI tools for research what their biggest concerns are, and hallucinations and citation problems come up fast. In fact, 64% of researchers cited potential inaccuracies and hallucinations as concerns preventing them using AI as much as they''d like in our global study. The more urgent question is how quickly institutions can adapt to realize AI’s benefits – and expand their capacity to improve lives. The post Why we were at AI for Good: grounding artificial intelligence in knowledge you can trust appeared first on AI for Good .',2.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "items" VALUES(620,'https://aiforgood.itu.int/from-open-data-to-local-impact-an-mcp-server-and-a-fellowship-for-social-impact-technology-leaders/','https://aiforgood.itu.int/from-open-data-to-local-impact-an-mcp-server-and-a-fellowship-for-social-impact-technology-leaders','From open data to local impact: An MCP server and a fellowship for social impact technology leaders','fromopendatatolocalimpactanmcpserverandafellowshipforsocialimpacttechnologyleaders','itu_ai4good','ITU AI for Good','en','2026-10-07T12:00:32Z','2026-10-17T08:55:20Z','How AWS is making scientific data discoverable and investing in the people who build where it matters most. The post From open data to local impact: An MCP server and a fellowship for social impact technology leaders appeared first on AI for Good .',1.0,'filtered_out',NULL,NULL);
